<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>com.berwilson.cron-portfolio-snapshot</string>
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/bin/zsh</string>
    <string>-c</string>
    <string>curl -sS -m 280 -H "Authorization: Bearer $(grep '^CRON_SECRET=' __APP_DIR__/.env.local | cut -d= -f2-)" http://localhost:3000/api/cron/portfolio-snapshot</string>
  </array>
  <!--
    Mondays at 05:30 — one row of the dashboard's own KPI figures, so a tile
    can say which way the number is going.

    ⚠ BEFORE THE CROWDED HOUR, DELIBERATELY. The week's figures should be the
    ones a human is about to be shown, so this lands an hour ahead of the
    06:20 curator and the 06:45 reminder rather than queueing behind them.

      05:30  THIS             (five aggregate reads, one upsert, no model)
      06:20  curator
      06:45  task reminder
      07:00  daily digest

    ⚠ NO MODEL CALL. LM Studio serves one request at a time and eight sweeps
    already contend for it (§12); this is arithmetic over rows that are already
    facts, and it must stay that way.

    ⚠ SAFE TO RUN TWICE. The row upserts on `captured_on`, so a deploy, a
    manual curl or a launchd catch-up after the box slept cannot double a
    week's delta. Run it by hand any time:
      curl -H "Authorization: Bearer $CRON_SECRET" localhost:3000/api/cron/portfolio-snapshot

    ⚠ WEEKLY IS THE SCHEDULE, NOT THE ASSUMPTION. The tile derives "vs last
    week" from the real gap between the two dates, so a missed Monday reads as
    "vs 14 days ago" rather than quietly claiming a week.
  -->
  <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
  <array>
    <dict><key>Weekday</key><integer>1</integer><key>Hour</key><integer>5</integer><key>Minute</key><integer>30</integer></dict>
  </array>
  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>__LOG_DIR__/cron-portfolio-snapshot.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>__LOG_DIR__/cron-portfolio-snapshot.log</string>
  <key>RunAtLoad</key>
  <false/>
</dict>
</plist>
